{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 4958062,
  "courseSlug": "remix-course",
  "courseTitle": "Remix.js - The Practical Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "34674476",
      "title": "Returning & Using Fetched Data",
      "lectureOrder": 23,
      "videoOrder": 19,
      "sourceHash": "06a7a2b21bc675269ffa1d42afbf36d7125453309f689e1e6c5a8ae8f4ace10d",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 4.17,
          "en": "Here I want to call getStoredNotes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.17,
          "end": 5.55,
          "en": "which is a never function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.55,
          "end": 7.92,
          "en": "We import from data/notes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.92,
          "end": 10.29,
          "en": "Actually, we are already importing it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.29,
          "end": 13.59,
          "en": "because we already used it here in the action as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.59,
          "end": 17.07,
          "en": "I'll use it again here and getStoredNotes returns a promise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.07,
          "end": 20.28,
          "en": "so I'll turn my loader into a async function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.28,
          "end": 23.91,
          "en": "Adjust like the action, it can be async or not async.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.91,
          "end": 25.62,
          "en": "Here, we need it to be async",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.62,
          "end": 29.85,
          "en": "because I want use the await keyword to get my notes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.85,
          "end": 32.163,
          "en": "which are stored in the notes.json file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.57,
          "end": 35.49,
          "en": "And then here, that's actually all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.49,
          "end": 36.99,
          "en": "I don't need to do anything else,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.99,
          "end": 40.59,
          "en": "I just want to retrieve my notes and now I need to pass them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.59,
          "end": 43.8,
          "en": "to this component because I want to output my notes there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.8,
          "end": 45.063,
          "en": "And how does this work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.05,
          "end": 49.08,
          "en": "Well, that's again the part where Remix makes sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.08,
          "end": 52.53,
          "en": "that these different ends and components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.53,
          "end": 55.14,
          "en": "and building blocks work together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.14,
          "end": 58.05,
          "en": "In our loader, we can simply return the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.05,
          "end": 60.81,
          "en": "that should be made available to the component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.81,
          "end": 63.69,
          "en": "So, to this component in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.69,
          "end": 66.51,
          "en": "Now technically, the data you return here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.51,
          "end": 69.99,
          "en": "in this loader is sent to the front end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.99,
          "end": 73.08,
          "en": "or to be very precise, this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.08,
          "end": 75.18,
          "en": "this NotesPage component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.18,
          "end": 77.55,
          "en": "can be rendered on the server side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 77.55,
          "end": 79.68,
          "en": "If it's the first request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 79.68,
          "end": 82.89,
          "en": "to this page by a given visitor, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 82.89,
          "end": 86.52,
          "en": "thereafter the visitor gets a single page application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 86.52,
          "end": 88.56,
          "en": "in which he or she navigates around.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 88.56,
          "end": 90.93,
          "en": "But for the first request, this is rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 90.93,
          "end": 94.59,
          "en": "on the server side and therefore this component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 94.59,
          "end": 97.923,
          "en": "might also actually be executed on the server side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 98.82,
          "end": 101.64,
          "en": "But if a user is already on our website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 101.64,
          "end": 104.28,
          "en": "and navigates around there, and is therefore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.28,
          "end": 107.07,
          "en": "in this single page application environment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 107.07,
          "end": 109.38,
          "en": "which Remix creates for them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 109.38,
          "end": 111.84,
          "en": "then Remix will just send requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 111.84,
          "end": 115.22999999999999,
          "en": "to the backend behind the scenes to fetch some new data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 115.22999999999999,
          "end": 117.21000000000001,
          "en": "And it will then color your loaders",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 117.21000000000001,
          "end": 121.08,
          "en": "on the backend because that code always runs on the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 121.08,
          "end": 123.81,
          "en": "and it will send these requests to the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 123.81,
          "end": 125.91,
          "en": "to the loader behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 125.91,
          "end": 127.29,
          "en": "Now I'm stressing this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 127.29,
          "end": 129.75,
          "en": "I'm emphasizing this because this means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 129.75,
          "end": 133.38,
          "en": "that the data returned by the loader sometimes needs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 133.38,
          "end": 136.89,
          "en": "to be sent from the backend to the front end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 136.89,
          "end": 139.44,
          "en": "So there must be a response sent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 139.44,
          "end": 141.42000000000002,
          "en": "from the backend to the front end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 141.42000000000002,
          "end": 144.57,
          "en": "And indeed, that's what Remix does behind the scenes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 144.57,
          "end": 147.633,
          "en": "it wraps this data into a response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 148.53,
          "end": 150.6,
          "en": "Now, you can also do this yourselves.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 150.6,
          "end": 154.26,
          "en": "You can return a new response using the standard",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 154.26,
          "end": 156.63,
          "en": "response constructor function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 156.63,
          "end": 160.68,
          "en": "the standard response class that's built into Node.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 160.68,
          "end": 163.38,
          "en": "So this is not a Remix feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 163.38,
          "end": 165.96,
          "en": "And you could pass your data to this response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 165.96,
          "end": 169.95,
          "en": "you could json stringify some data, like your notes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 169.95,
          "end": 174.213,
          "en": "because that data must be converted to json format.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 175.32,
          "end": 179.25,
          "en": "And you could then add a second value, a second argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 179.25,
          "end": 181.59,
          "en": "to this response constructor function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 181.59,
          "end": 184.59,
          "en": "to add some extra headers so that you, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 184.59,
          "end": 187.83,
          "en": "can set the content type header and set this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 187.83,
          "end": 190.32,
          "en": "to application/json.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 190.32,
          "end": 193.35,
          "en": "That's an alternative to sending back the data like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 193.35,
          "end": 196.32,
          "en": "And that's in the end what Remix does under the hood.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 196.32,
          "end": 198.3,
          "en": "Though, of course, this approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 198.3,
          "end": 201.78,
          "en": "where you just return the notes is much shorter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 201.78,
          "end": 204.12,
          "en": "But there also is a shorter alternative",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 204.12,
          "end": 206.01,
          "en": "to what I just showed you in cases where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 206.01,
          "end": 209.61,
          "en": "you still want to send back a response manually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 209.61,
          "end": 212.31,
          "en": "Remix offers a json function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 212.31,
          "end": 216.42000000000002,
          "en": "which must be imported from remix-run/node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 216.42000000000002,
          "end": 220.68,
          "en": "And that json function actually takes your raw data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 220.68,
          "end": 222.81,
          "en": "and converts it to a json response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 222.81,
          "end": 225.63,
          "en": "behind the scenes, setting that content type header",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 225.63,
          "end": 228.06,
          "en": "behind the scenes as well, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 228.06,
          "end": 230.04,
          "en": "So this, all the returns are response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 230.04,
          "end": 231.39,
          "en": "instead of the raw data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 231.39,
          "end": 235.02,
          "en": "But it's an easier way of returning such a json response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 235.02,
          "end": 236.79,
          "en": "And indeed, that is what Remix will do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 236.79,
          "end": 240.213,
          "en": "behind the scenes if you just return raw data like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 241.11,
          "end": 243.6,
          "en": "Now, here I'll stick to returning raw data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 243.6,
          "end": 245.79,
          "en": "and I won't use this json function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 245.79,
          "end": 248.46,
          "en": "but I wanted to show this alternative to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 248.46,
          "end": 251.58,
          "en": "because it is important to understand what Remix does",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 251.58,
          "end": 253.83,
          "en": "behind the scenes, and what you could",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 253.83,
          "end": 256.26,
          "en": "instead of returning the raw data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 256.26,
          "end": 258.723,
          "en": "But here I'll simply return my notes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 259.71,
          "end": 261.39,
          "en": "I return my notes here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 261.39,
          "end": 265.5,
          "en": "and in this component we now get access to these notes here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 265.5,
          "end": 267.3,
          "en": "to the data returned by the loader",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 267.3,
          "end": 270.6,
          "en": "by using a special hook provided by Remix.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 270.6,
          "end": 272.853,
          "en": "The useLoaderData hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 274.26,
          "end": 278.13,
          "en": "This hook is imported from remix-run/react",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 278.13,
          "end": 280.62,
          "en": "and this hook simply gives us access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 280.62,
          "end": 282.603,
          "en": "to the data returned by the loader.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 283.65,
          "end": 287.1,
          "en": "Now, very important, the data returned here is serialized,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 287.1,
          "end": 290.52,
          "en": "it's temporarily converted to a json string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 290.52,
          "end": 293.67,
          "en": "so you can't return any rich objects here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 293.67,
          "end": 295.53,
          "en": "I mean you can, but any methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 295.53,
          "end": 297.42,
          "en": "or anything like that will get lost.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 297.42,
          "end": 300.45,
          "en": "You just get the plain data and that's what",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 300.45,
          "end": 302.82,
          "en": "you get here with useLoaderData.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 302.82,
          "end": 305.52,
          "en": "So here I get my notes, my array of notes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 305.52,
          "end": 307.38,
          "en": "and in this case nothing will be lost",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 307.38,
          "end": 310.23,
          "en": "because my notes are just a bunch of strings in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 310.23,
          "end": 312.783,
          "en": "and that is perfectly serializable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 313.98,
          "end": 317.97,
          "en": "And then the notes here can be passed to the notes prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 317.97,
          "end": 319.983,
          "en": "of the note list component like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 321.66,
          "end": 323.97,
          "en": "And that is all we have to do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 323.97,
          "end": 326.55,
          "en": "to load data for this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 326.55,
          "end": 329.64,
          "en": "And this loader, as mentioned, will be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 329.64,
          "end": 331.623,
          "en": "whenever a user visits this page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 332.64,
          "end": 335.97,
          "en": "If we already visited a never page, and we then click a link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 335.97,
          "end": 338.15999999999997,
          "en": "so that we are redirected to this page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 338.15999999999997,
          "end": 341.85,
          "en": "Remix will behind the scenes, execute a loader on the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 341.85,
          "end": 344.67,
          "en": "and make the data available on the front end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 344.67,
          "end": 347.49,
          "en": "We don't have to worry about anything regarding that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 347.49,
          "end": 350.88,
          "en": "and we don't have to send our own request to a backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 350.88,
          "end": 352.59000000000003,
          "en": "or do anything like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 352.59000000000003,
          "end": 355.47,
          "en": "Instead, that's one of the advantages of Remix.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 355.47,
          "end": 359.613,
          "en": "It seamlessly blends front end and backend together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 360.75,
          "end": 363.42,
          "en": "If we save this and we go back,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 363.42,
          "end": 364.74,
          "en": "we should therefore see this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 364.74,
          "end": 368.52,
          "en": "first note here, below this input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 368.52,
          "end": 369.57,
          "en": "And I'll zoom out a bit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 369.57,
          "end": 371.52,
          "en": "so that we can see it a bit better.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 371.52,
          "end": 372.84,
          "en": "Here's this note.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 372.84,
          "end": 374.22,
          "en": "It's not clickable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 374.22,
          "end": 375.72,
          "en": "I just have this animation here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 375.72,
          "end": 377.793,
          "en": "but this is the note we added before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 379.23,
          "end": 380.55,
